               {"text": "dehī iti. dehī śarīrī nityaṃ sarvadā sarvāvasthāsu avadhyaḥ niravayavatvāt nityatvāt ca tatra avadhyo'yaṃ dehe śarīre sarvasya sarvagatatvāt sthāvarādiṣu sthito'pi. sarvasya prāṇijātasya dehe vadhyamāne'pi ayaṃ dehī na vadhyaḥ yasmāt tasmāt bhīṣmādīni sarvāṇi bhūtāni uddiśya na tvaṃ śocituṃ arhasi.", "tr": "'This embodied one…' The embodied one, the indweller of the body, is ever — at all times, in all states — beyond harm, because it has no parts and is eternal. It is beyond harm in the body of every creature; since it is all-pervading, it dwells in the unmoving and all other beings too. Since this embodied one is not slain even when the body of any living being is slain, you should not grieve for any being, Bhīṣma or anyone else."},
