               {"text": "yāmiti ḥ– yāmimāṃ vakṣyamāṇāṃ, puṣpitāṃ puṣpitavṛkṣa iva śobhamānāṃ śrūyamāṇa ramaṇīyāṃ, vācaṃ vākyalakṣaṇāṃ pravadanti, ke? avipaścitaḥ alpamedhasaḥ avivekinaḥ ityarthaḥ, vedavādaratāḥ bahvarthavādaphalasādhanaprakāśakeṣu vedavākyeṣu ratāḥ he! pārtha! na anyat svargapaśvādiphalasādhanebhyaḥ karmabhyaḥ asti ityevaṃ vādinaḥ vadanaśīlāḥ", "tr": "'This flowery speech…' This speech, about to be described, flowery — beautiful like a tree in flower, pleasing to hear — the undiscerning speak, those of little intelligence, without discrimination: that is the meaning. They delight in the words of the Veda — in Vedic passages that set out many eulogies, fruits and means — Pārtha, and they declare that there is nothing else beyond the rites that are means to fruits such as heaven and cattle."},
