               {"text": "dhyāyata iti – dhyāyataḥ cintayataḥ, viṣayān śabdādiviṣaya viśeṣān ālocayataḥ, puṃsaḥ puruṣasya, saṅgaḥ āsaktiḥ, prītiḥ, teṣu viṣayeṣu upajāyate utpadyate. saṅgāt prīteḥ sañjāyate samutpadyate, kāmaḥ tṛṣṇā. kāmāt kutaścit pratihatāt, krodhaḥ abhijāyate.", "tr": "'When a man dwells on objects…' When a man dwells on — thinks about, contemplates — objects, the particular objects such as sound, attachment, fondness, for them arises. From attachment, fondness, desire, thirst, is born. From desire, when it is thwarted by something, anger arises."},
